From: hanbang <hanbang@localhost>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 01:46:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] GG Dual: option description uses ',' instead of ';'

RetroArch splits a core option description from its value list at the
first ';', so gg_dual_link showed values like "restart); on" in the menu
and rewrote the per-game .opt with that value. Only the description text
changes (one byte, ';' -> ','). Same fix as NGP Dual 0005.

(Reconstructed 2026-10-29: this change was built into the core on
2026-10-22 straight from the working tree and was never committed. The
diff below is `git diff` of that working tree against commit 3ef1895
(= 302fe82 + patches 0001 and 0002).)
---
 dual/libretro_dual.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dual/libretro_dual.c b/dual/libretro_dual.c
index c0c57f4..56b3896 100644
--- a/dual/libretro_dual.c
+++ b/dual/libretro_dual.c
@@ -702,7 +702,7 @@ void retro_set_environment(retro_environment_t env)
    /* 메뉴 글씨: 기기 레트로아크 글꼴에 한글이 없을 수 있어 영어(다른 Dual 과 같음) */
    static const struct retro_variable vars[] = {
       { "gg_dual_screen", "Screen and sound (host/solo = 1P, guest = 2P); 1P|2P" },
-      { "gg_dual_link", "2P Game Gear on the Gear-to-Gear cable (off = solo, one console; restart); on|off" },
+      { "gg_dual_link", "2P Game Gear on the Gear-to-Gear cable (off = solo, one console, restart); on|off" },
       { NULL, NULL },
    };
    static const struct retro_controller_description pads[] = {
